  "step_3": "The decision reason requires considering the maximum magnitude outcome (2500 vs. 2400) and weighting it by its probability (A: 2500 × 0.33 = 825, B: 2400 × 0.34 = 816), and preferring the higher weighted value. However, the individual did not consider the magnitude of the outcomes at all, nor did they compute or reference any weighting of the maximum outcome by probability. Instead, the individual focused solely on the probability of winning (34% vs. 33%) and chose Lottery B based on that. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The information considered (probability of winning) differs from the required information (maximum magnitude outcome weighted by probability). The justification (choosing based on higher probability) does not match the rule of the decision reason (weighting maximum outcome by probability).",
